ame":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-21T19:24:33Z","updated_at":"2026-08-22T16:36:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nrepro in v4.8.dev3.official [51105ccbe]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev3 - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 22 May 2026 19:25:09 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Single-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (radeonsi, phoenix, ACO, DRM 3.64, 7.0.9-arch2-1) - AMD Ryzen 7 8745HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 28.18 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf I set a breakpoint in the script editor, nothing indicates that I have \"skip breakpoints\" enabled if I have the debugger tab minimized. This leads to confusion for the user thinking that their breakpoint is never hit.\n\nI think these icons should be kept in sync, or maybe a `!` could be added next to breakpoints in the script editor.\n\n<img width=\"886\" height=\"594\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b9f79d4c-dd80-49aa-93a5-6734cec67636\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Enable skip breakpoints \n- Make a breakpoint\n- Minimize the debugger window\n- There is no way to see that breakpoints are disabled\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122704/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godo